Phantom-WG Modern — Update Guide
==================================

Standard Update:
  ./tools/prod.sh update

  This pulls the latest code from upstream and restarts all services.
  Environment files (.env, .env.daemon, .env.auth-service) and
  docker-compose.override.yml are always preserved.

  Alternatively:
    git pull
    ./tools/prod.sh restart

Local Changes:
  Server-specific changes (ports, resource limits, extra volumes) belong in
  docker-compose.override.yml. It is not tracked by git, so updates leave
  it as it is.

Compose Lock:
  An update stops if docker-compose.yml has local changes. To update with
  them in place, use compose lock:

    ./tools/prod.sh compose lock

  The lock persists across sessions. A release that changes docker-compose.yml
  itself still stops the update: unlock, move your changes to
  docker-compose.override.yml, and update again.

    ./tools/prod.sh compose status    Check if locked
    ./tools/prod.sh compose unlock    Release to pull upstream changes

  How it works:
    Compose lock uses git update-index --assume-unchanged to tell git
    to ignore local changes to docker-compose.yml during pull.

Dependency Updates:
  Registry source: the release pins its images, pull them and start:

    ./tools/prod.sh pull
    ./tools/prod.sh up

  Build source: if requirements.txt or a Dockerfile changed after an update:

    ./tools/prod.sh rebuild
    ./tools/prod.sh up

  This rebuilds the images from scratch with the new dependencies.

Version Check:
  ./tools/prod.sh show-versions

  Shows the current daemon version and bridge versions running
  inside the container.

Rollback:
  To roll back to a previous version:

    git fetch --tags
    git checkout v1.0.7
    ./tools/prod.sh restart

  If the images may have changed between versions:

    git checkout v1.0.7
    ./tools/prod.sh pull       (registry source)
    ./tools/prod.sh rebuild    (build source)
    ./tools/prod.sh up

  This creates a detached HEAD state — you are pinned to that tag.
  To resume receiving updates, switch back to main:

    git checkout main
    ./tools/prod.sh update

  Environment files and runtime data are unaffected by rollback.

Hard Reset:
  ./tools/prod.sh hard-reset

  Destroys ALL data: secrets, auth database, client databases,
  and Docker volumes. Requires typing 'yes' to confirm. Environment files
  and docker-compose.override.yml stay.

  After hard reset, run setup again:
    ./tools/prod.sh setup

What Gets Preserved on Update:
  docker-compose.override.yml Always preserved (not tracked by git)
  .env                       Always preserved (not tracked by git)
  .env.daemon                Always preserved (not tracked by git)
  .env.auth-service          Always preserved (not tracked by git)
  docker-compose.yml         Preserved only when compose lock is active
  container-data/            Always preserved (runtime data, not in git)

What Gets Updated:
  phantom_daemon/            Daemon source code
  services/auth-service/     Auth service source
  services/react-spa/dist/   Web dashboard build
  services/nginx/            Reverse proxy config
  tools/                     Production CLI, libraries and image pins
  Dockerfile                 Image definition
  requirements.txt           Python dependencies